    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Superb three bedroom semi-detached red brick home with a south facing garden ideally located in a quiet cul-de-sac with views of Dublin Bay.\n\nThis exceptional property overlooks a large green area and has a paved front driveway and garden with side access to the rear of the home. A stained glass front door opens to an entrance hall with a tiled floor, understairs storage and a guest w.c. To the right of the hallway is an open plan kitchen & dining area with splashback tiling and plenty of counter & cupboard space. The spacious light filled living room enjoys laminate floors, a gas fireplace and a sliding door to the amazing south east facing back garden and paved patio. Comfy carpet on the stairs and landing leads to three bedrooms and the family bathroom. The master bedroom is positioned to rear of the home and comes with carpet flooring, ample fitted wardrobes, wall mounted shelving and also incorporates a stylish ensuite. There are two bedrooms to the front of the property with carpet, fitted wardrobes and views of Dublin Bay. The generous sized family bathroom has shelving and a Velux window. The hotpress and large convertible attic are accessed via the landing.\n\nVevay Crescent is a mature sought after development with a large green area overlooking Dublin Bay. Just a short stroll from the town centre, there are plenty of amenities such as shops, cafes, restaurants and bars in the area. There are also lots of sports clubs, parks, schools and playgrounds. Bray DART station is within walking distance which makes the city centre easily accessible. Bray Beach & Promenade are also within walking distance making this an ideal home by the coast.\n\nFeatures:\nYear of construction 1998\nCul-de-sac\nSemi-detached\nRed brick façade\nSouth east garden\nOverlooking large green & Dublin Bay\nOpen plan kitchen & dining\nGas fireplace\nFitted wardrobes\nSought after location"
      },
